---
/** The honest-limits block: what we're not, the strongest trust section on the site. */
---

<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 mt-20">
  <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">What we're not, and why that's a good thing</h2>
  <div class="mt-5 text-lg text-ink-soft space-y-4">
    <p>
      We're <strong class="text-ink">not lawyers</strong>, but we'll tell you what's normal here
      and when it's worth talking to one. We're <strong class="text-ink">not doctors</strong>,
      but we'll help you find one who speaks English. We're
      <strong class="text-ink">not the police, the university, or the immigration office</strong>,
      and we can't represent you officially, but we can help you prepare, understand the
      process, and sometimes come along.
    </p>
    <p>
      For visa, permit, or legal-status questions, we'll always point you to official
      sources and qualified people. That work is too important for amateurs, including us.
    </p>
    <p>
      We're <strong class="text-ink">not an emergency service.</strong> In any real emergency,
      call <strong class="text-ink">112</strong> first. Always.
    </p>
    <p>
      We don't promise to solve everything. Nobody honestly can. We promise you'll always
      have someone local, kind, and competent to ask, and you'll always leave knowing what
      to do next.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
